-- title:
--   Bezoutian contraction bijective: reduction to algebraically closed fields
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring (in a universe $u$), let $m$ be a natural number and let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to R[x_1,\dots,x_m]$ be a family of $m$ polynomials in $m$ variables such that $A := R[x_1,\dots,x_m]/(f_1,\dots,f_m)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $f$, is a finite free $R$-module. Let $a_{ij} \in R[x]\otimes_R R[x]$ be a matrix of Bezoutian coefficients, that is, $f_i\otimes 1 - 1\otimes f_i = \sum_j a_{ij}\,(x_j\otimes 1 - 1\otimes x_j)$ for each $i$. For a ring $S$, a family $g$ of $m$ polynomials in $m$ variables over $S$ and a matrix $b$ over $S[x]\otimes_S S[x]$, write $\theta_{g,b}$ for the $S$-linear map from $\mathrm{Hom}_S(S[x]/(g),S)$ to $S[x]/(g)$ obtained by sending $\varphi$ to the contraction in the first tensor factor, by $\varphi$, of the image of $\det(b)$ under the quotient map $S[x]\otimes_S S[x] \to S[x]/(g) \otimes_S S[x]/(g)$ (formally: `LinearMap.rTensor` applied to $\varphi$ followed by the identification `TensorProduct.lid`). Assume that for every algebraically closed field $K$ in the universe $u$, every family $g$ of $m$ polynomials in $m$ variables over $K$ whose quotient $K[x]/(g)$ is a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space, and every matrix $b$ over $K[x]\otimes_K K[x]$ satisfying the Bezoutian identity $g_i\otimes 1 - 1\otimes g_i = \sum_j b_{ij}(x_j\otimes 1 - 1\otimes x_j)$, the map $\theta_{g,b}$ is bijective. Then $\theta_{f,a} : \mathrm{Hom}_R(A,R) \to A$ is bijective.
--
--   The map $\theta_{f,a}$ is the Scheja–Storch contraction attached to a square presentation and a choice of Bezoutian matrix; its bijectivity expresses that the image of $\det(a)$ in $A\otimes_R A$ is a perfect duality element, so that $A$ carries a canonical trace form and is Gorenstein over $R$. This statement is the descent step: finiteness and freeness of $A$ let the construction be compared with its base changes to the residue fields $R/\mathfrak m$ and their algebraic closures, and bijectivity over $R$ is deduced from bijectivity over algebraically closed fields by way of [`LinearMap.bijective_of_forall_bijective_baseChange_quotient_maximal`](thm.html#LinearMap.bijective_of_forall_bijective_baseChange_quotient_maximal). It is used by [`Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_square_presentation`](thm.html#Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_square_presentation).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_forall_field.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
